    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Coma Divine (Recorded Live in Rome) is Porcupine Tree’s first official live album, captured across three March 1997 performances at the Frontiera in Rome and released by Delerium Records later that year. It presents the band in a transitional but commanding period, drawing on material from their early psychedelic and progressive rock catalog while highlighting the growing sophistication that would soon define their wider reputation.\n\nThe set is notable for its polished presentation: although recorded live, it includes some studio vocal overdubs and careful mixing to compensate for technical issues and performance imperfections. The result is a spacious, atmospheric document that captures Porcupine Tree’s blend of trippy textures, expansive instrumentation, and melodic intensity, while also serving as a snapshot of the momentum the group had built around Signify.",
